            <ArticleTitle>A tonsillolith seen on MRI.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>205-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of a large tonsillolith visualized by magnetic resonance imaging is presented. Although otolaryngologists are well aware of this entity, few radiologists are. The importance of distinguishing tonsilloliths from other structures by MRI is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
